> Considering last fall�[�]s wet weather and the soggy fields this spring, farmers wonder about using inoculants on soy[bean] seed in 2010. Should you use a rhizobium inoculant? Or, is there[ enough] of the nitrogen-fixing bacteria, Bradyrhiz[obia] japonicum, remaining in the soil?
